  "notes": "Boot a Black Rose ROM from an empty NVRAM with the coin door open (public 22 released) and PinMAME's built-in mechanisms disabled; the scenario names no game. Leave the fresh-NVRAM loop with Escape and open the service menu. Start T.12 FLIPPER COIL TEST (the L-4 ROM's twelfth test; the manual's list predates it) and step it with Up until it wraps. In repeat mode the ROM pulses the selected flipper winding and prints its name, number and wire colours, pairing each name with the public address PinMAME published. T.12 must pulse 45 after it starts. Three frames 0.35 s apart are taken at every step.",
